      "created_at": "2025-11-16T18:00:26Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-11-16T18:02:36Z",
      "body": "I was thinking a getter/Proxy with a file references manager might be useful for making reference updates painless, this would get rid of one of having to find/store every node and updating their file reference. \n\nWould be stored in the SQLite db ofc\n\nAny changes to them (e.g. by a new event that might provide a newer reference to an expired one) could be intercepted by the dispatcher internally and the reference could be updated there.\n\nWhat's your opinion on this?\n\n",
